==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kaolan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Kaolan Tatalan''' at level 30 using Catfruit and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Kaolan Pasalan can be used similarly to [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togelan Pasalan]], a vulnerable attacker with very high range and damage. It is incredibly high to be specific, with 3k DPS at a whopping 710 range. The damage per hit isn't that bad either due to the shorter overall attack cycle. Its massive coverage allows it to safely stay in the back and constantly chip away at threats while your frontline takes the heat. It also offers some crowd-controlling potential, though due to its stats, it can be safely said this unit relies more on damaging threats, as 20% chance to [[Knockback]] is too low for it to be effective, even with the [[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]] factored in. These mostly act as a bonus, not doing much for the unit but not bad to have either. Just be wary in stages with [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance]], [[:Category:Omni Strike Enemies|Omni Strike]], [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave]] or [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge]] enemies, as it can easily be hit by these abilities.

Easily the best aspect of Kaolan Pasalan is [[Sigh of Relief (Combo)|Sigh of Relief]], a 2-slot Research (M) [[Cat Combo|Combo]] with [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]. This is the same efficiency as [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]], reducing unit cooldowns by 1.73 seconds.

==='''True Form'''===
The most notable buff gained by Kaolan Tatalan is the addition of [[Colossus Slayer]], giving it a viable niche in many Colossus [[Gauntlet]]s that don't feature enemies with high pierce. It handedly outranges [[Baron Seal]] and [[Le'Grim]] as well as their support, and can even be used against [[Archangel Exiel]] so long as you have a constant line of Wave Shield units to protect it from [[Bore Jr.]]. [[Mega-Mooth]] and [[Big Peng Z]]'s later stages do feature a large quantity of Zombies that can easily burrow into Kaolan Tatalan and kill it, but its increased Mini-Surge level gives it a better opportunity to Knockback or stagger said enemies more easily while increasing its DPS to ~9.7k at Lv.30. Similarly, it's not as viable against [[Omens]] until [[Johnnyleon]] has been eliminated.

[[Immune to Surge]] is also invaluable for a super-backliner like Kaolan Tatalan, giving it more use in Aku-centric stages that consistently spam Death Surges. Any resistance to pierce helps it immensely with its low HP and knockback count, especially in mixed [[Uncanny Legends]] stages like [[Hell's Crater]].

Overall, a fine True Form with improvements all across the board that make it far better at what it does.

