==Trivia==
*''Kao'' (顔) is the Japanese word for face, referring to how its Evolved and True Forms attacks by disconnecting its head to spew noxious miasma with its face on it.
*Kaolan Tatalan's name may be a combination of ''Kaolan Pasalan'' and 戦い ''tatakai'' (battle).
*Kaolan Tatalan's description and design reference [[wikipedia:Taira no Masakado|Taira no Masakado]], a samurai who was killed by an arrow to the head and decapitated, but is rumored to have lived on as a disembodied head searching for his body. The unit's hairstyle is similar to [[wikia:megamitensei:Masakado|Masakado]]'s from some of the ''[[wikipedia:Megami Tensei|Megami Tensei]]'' games.
**Kaolan Tatalan is the only [[True Form]] [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Luga]] to primarily reference Japanese history and mythology rather than a specific piece of media.
*Prior to [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]], its Evolved Form did not follow the usual naming scheme for Evolved [[Nekoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lugas]], being called Kaoluga Pasalan rather than Kaolan Pasalan. This was likely a typo, as its Japanese name has always been カオランパサラン ''Kaoran Pasaran'' (Kaolan Pasalan).
**[[Papaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Papaluga]] and Kaoluga are also the only Lugas whose True Form's English names don't have "Pasalan" in them.

